The AC-3 / E-AC-3 decoder (crates/ac3, the rivet-ac3 repository,
https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-ac3, under the same licence as the
H.264 / H.265 decoders) is original code by the same author, written from
ATSC A/52:2018 including its Annex E. It does not include or derive from any
other AC-3 or E-AC-3 decoder; its normative tables were transcribed from the
A/52:2018 PDF, each naming the spec table and page it came from. libavcodec
was used only as a black box (the ffmpeg command-line tool) to make and
decode test streams. AC-3 and E-AC-3 may be subject to patent licensing in
some jurisdictions. Dolby, Dolby Digital and Dolby Digital Plus are
trademarks of Dolby Laboratories; this software is not affiliated with Dolby.

