The DTS Coherent Acoustics core decoder (crates/dts, the rivet-dts repository,
https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-dts, under the same licence as the
H.264 / H.265 decoders) is original code by the same author, written from
ETSI TS 102 114 V1.6.1, which ETSI publishes free of charge, with its
normative tables transcribed from that PDF and cross-checked against V1.2.1.
It does not include or derive from any other DTS decoder (not libavcodec, not
libdcadec); the two code books no ETSI edition prints are not included. ffmpeg
was used only as a black box to make and decode test streams. DTS Coherent
Acoustics was patented by DTS, Inc.; "DTS" is a trademark of its owner, used
only to name the format.

