The Apple ProRes decoder and encoder (crates/prores, the rivet-prores
repository, https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-prores, under the same
licence as the H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original code by the same author,
written from SMPTE RDD 36:2022, "Apple ProRes Bitstream Syntax and Decoding
Process", which SMPTE publishes free of charge. They do not include or derive
from any other ProRes encoder or decoder: no other implementation's code was
read, and none was run to make or check anything. The tables are reproduced
from RDD 36; the encoder's target bit rates are Apple's published figures.
Apple and ProRes are trademarks of Apple Inc.; this software is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Apple, which runs a licensing programme for
ProRes products. This software grants no rights under any Apple patent or
trademark and makes no claim about whether a licence is needed.

