The VP8 decoder and encoder (crates/vp8, the rivet-vp8 repository,
https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-vp8, under the same licence as the
H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original code by the same author, written from
RFC 6386, its prose and tables. They do not include or derive from any other
VP8 implementation: not libvpx, not libavcodec, and not the reference decoder
whose source RFC 6386 attaches (its section 20), which was not read. The
decoder is verified against the WebM project's VP8 comprehensive test
vectors, used as data; no implementation was run to make or check anything.
Implementations of VP8 may be covered by patents; this software grants no
patent rights and makes no claim about whether a licence is needed.

