The MPEG-2 video (ITU-T H.262) decoder and encoder (crates/mpeg2, the
rivet-mpeg2 repository, https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-mpeg2,
under the same licence as the H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original code by
the same author, written from ITU-T Recommendation H.262 (02/2000) and, for
the MPEG-1 points H.262 summarises in its Annex D.9, ISO/IEC 11172-2. They do
not include or derive from any other MPEG-2 or MPEG-1 encoder or decoder
(not libavcodec, libmpeg2 or the MPEG Software Simulation Group's code);
the normative tables are reproduced from the Recommendation. The decoder is
verified against the ISO/IEC 13818-4 conformance bitstreams, used as data
and not redistributed; no other implementation was run to make or check test
data. MPEG-2 video has been subject to patent licensing in some
jurisdictions, through a programme Via LA administers; this software grants
no patent rights and makes no claim about whether a licence is needed.

