The MPEG-4 Part 2 Visual decoder and encoder (crates/mpeg4, the rivet-mpeg4
repository, https://github.com/rivet-transcoder/rivet-mpeg4, under the same
licence as the H.264 / H.265 decoders) are original code by the same author,
written from ISO/IEC 14496-2 and, for the short video header, ITU-T H.263,
with IEEE Std 1180-1990 for the IDCT accuracy test. They do not include or
derive from any other MPEG-4 Part 2 or H.263 encoder or decoder (not
libavcodec, Xvid, DivX or the MPEG-4 reference software), none of which was
read or run; the normative tables are the standard's data, transcribed. The
decoder is checked against other encoders' sample streams, used as data
only and not redistributed. MPEG-4 Visual may be subject to patent licensing
in some jurisdictions, through a programme Via LA administers; this software
grants no patent rights and makes no claim about whether a licence is needed.

